 # Static support boundaries
 
-This project isolates open tool maps, helper-built session instructions, initialization-sensitive subclasses, and ordinary function-tool delegation outside Cloudflare AIChatAgent's supported static relationships.
+The canonical agent registry keeps only relationships proved inside each selected `AIChatAgent` class boundary.
+
+- `support` has a direct instruction loader, but its complete request tool set is unresolved because the direct generation call spreads runtime-selected tools.
+- `step-support` has no proved instruction loader because `prepareStep` can replace the request instruction.
+- `delegating-support` has an ordinary function tool whose implementation references `StepSupportAgent`; that reference proves neither a handoff nor a routing target.
+
+Indirect generation, array output, and initialization-sensitive executable fields remain outside the registry. Deployment responsibilities are recorded in [the Cloudflare runtime guide](../docs/cloudflare-runtime.md).

