+# Cloudflare runtime guide
+
+The canonical registry describes static relationships, not a deployable Worker. The deployment owner must:
+
+- export each registered `AIChatAgent` class from the Worker entry point and map deployment-selected Durable Object namespace bindings to those classes;
+- add the classes to a Wrangler Durable Object migration using `new_sqlite_classes` before first deployment;
+- configure the provider binding and credentials that resolve `openai/gpt-5` (the source does not prove a binding name or secret source); and
+- own the Worker name, compatibility settings, routes, environment configuration, and deployment command.
+
+The indirect-generation, array-output, and initialization-sensitive classes are not registered deployment targets.
